// Title: PUA - CsExec Execution
// Sigma ID: d08a2711-ee8b-4323-bdec-b7d85e892b31
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-22 | Modified: 2023-02-21
// ATT&CK: resource-development, T1587.001, execution, T1569.002
// Description: Detects the use of the lesser known remote execution tool named CsExec a PsExec alternative
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/malcomvetter/CSExec
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/05/09/ransomware-as-a-service-understanding-the-cybercrime-gig-economy-and-how-to-protect-yourself/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_csexec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\csexec.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "csexec"
